    "summary": "From the church in Shreveport and New Orleans to New York in 1992: Kenny Garrett, Joshua Redman, his own Fellowship Band from 1997, Wayne Shorter's quartet from 2000, and records with Joni Mitchell, Bob Dylan, Emmylou Harris, Daniel Lanois and Norah Jones. A huge range of dynamics, the ride light and 'dancing along the top of the time' (Todd Bishop), the comping in triplets between the snare and the bass drum, 'always playing counter lines'."
